 // Deletion + undo helpers","refToolCallId":"toolu_0199nWvrWbhN6khrYRXgiErN"},{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have successfully implemented comprehensive filtering across all the major screens in the cattle management app. Here's a summary of what I've accomplished:

## Summary of Changes Made

### 1. **Dashboard Screen** ✅
- Updated to show only **active cattle** in total head count
- Removed the separate "Active" count from overview cards
- All statistics now reflect active cattle only by default

### 2. **Cattle Screen (CowsScreen)** ✅
- **Default filter**: Shows only active cattle
- **Multi-select filtering** for:
 - Status (Active, Sold, Deceased)
 - Classification (Bull, Cow, Steer, Heifer, Calf)
 - Gender (Male, Female)
 - Pasture (all available pastures)
- **Enhanced UI**: Expandable filter section with filter chips
- **Clear filters** functionality with visual indicators

### 3. **Pastures Screen** ✅
- Updated pasture cards to show **"Total Head"** instead of "Cows"
- Added **classification breakdown** on each pasture card (e.g., "Bull: 2 • Cow: 5 • Calf: 3")
- Only counts **active cattle** in all statistics
- Enhanced data model (`PastureWithCowCount`) to include classification breakdown

### 4. **Activities Screen** ✅
- **Default filter**: Shows activities for active cattle only
- **Multi-select filtering** for:
 - Cattle Status (Active, Sold, Deceased)
 - Animal Type (Bull, Cow, Steer, Heifer, Calf)
 - Gender (Male, Female)
 - Pasture (all available pastures)
 - Activity Type (all available activity types)
- **Enhanced UI**: Expandable filter section in top bar
- **Smart filtering**: Activities are filtered based on the cattle's current attributes

### 5. **Working List Screen** ✅
- **Default filter**: Shows only active cattle
- **Multi-select filtering** for:
 - Status (Active, Sold, Deceased)
 - Classification (Bull, Cow, Steer, Heifer, Calf)
 - Gender (Male, Female)
 - Pasture (all available pastures)
- **Enhanced UI**: Modern filter chip interface
- **Progress tracking**: Shows checked items progress

## Key Features Implemented

### **Consistent Default Behavior**
- All screens now default to showing **active cattle only**
- Users must explicitly select other statuses to see sold/deceased animals

### **Multi-Select Filtering**
- All filter categories support multiple selections
- Filter chips show selected state visually
- Easy toggle on/off functionality

### **Smart Filter Management**
- **Clear All Filters** button appears when non-default filters are active
- **Visual indicators** show when filters are applied
- **Automatic fallback** to active status when no status filters selected

### **Enhanced Data Display**
- Pasture cards show detailed breakdowns by animal type
- Consistent "Total Head" terminology throughout
- Only active animals counted in all statistics

### **Improved User Experience**
- **Expandable filter sections** to save screen space
- **Filter chips** for easy visual identification
- **Consistent UI patterns** across all screens

